flowchart TB

  SEAM["THE WHOLE SEAM BETWEEN THE TWO PATHS IS TWO THINGS<br/>systems/createSceneRenderer.ts — one function, one branch, the fallback behind a dynamic import()<br/>so a browser with WebGPU never downloads, parses or executes a byte of the second renderer<br/>systems/SceneRendererHandle.ts — one interface, naming no graphics API<br/>deleting the fallback later is deleting src/webgl/ and the catch"]

  SHARED["SHARED — everything that is not graphics API code<br/>not one GPUDevice, GPURenderPassEncoder,<br/>WebGL2RenderingContext or WebGLTexture appears in any of it<br/><br/>shapes/ the scene graph · scene/ picking, culling, selection<br/>events/ · input/ · camera/ · math/ · svg/<br/>render/gather.ts — visibility, depth, lanes,<br/>the opaque split, the run merge<br/>render/meshFormat · textFormat · imageFormat · shadowFormat<br/>the byte layouts, and the offset constants both shader<br/>languages interpolate<br/>render/drawOrder · opacity · stroke · contours · shadowMath<br/>text/layout.ts — the shaper<br/>render/capture.ts — the backend-neutral capture arithmetic"]

  subgraph GPUP["webgpu/ — THE PRIMARY PATH"]
    GPU1["GpuContext · FrameRenderer · SceneRenderer"]
    GPU2["lanes/ MeshBatcher · TextBatcher · ImageBatcher · ShadowBatcher"]
    GPU3["pipelines/ · layouts.ts · vertexLayouts.ts · depthFormat.ts"]
    GPU4["shaders/ *.wgsl.ts"]
    GPU5["MSDFFontBook · MSDFFontLibrary · ImageTexture · ShadowAtlas · CaptureTarget"]
  end

  subgraph GLP["webgl/ — A SECOND, SELF-CONTAINED IMPLEMENTATION"]
    GL1["Gl2Context · GlSceneRenderer"]
    GL2["lanes/ GlMeshBatcher · GlTextBatcher · GlImageBatcher · GlShadowBatcher"]
    GL3["GlProgram · GlObjectTexture"]
    GL4["shaders/ *.glsl.ts<br/>a template string interpolating the SAME<br/>OBJECT_*_OFFSET constants the WGSL does"]
    GL5["GlMSDFFontBook · GlMSDFFontLibrary · GlImageTexture · GlShadowAtlas · GlCaptureTarget"]
  end

  SAME["THE SAME PICTURE, BOTH WAYS<br/>same scene objects · same picking, culling and z-order answers · 4x MSAA on both<br/>all four lanes implemented, the shadow bake included: silhouette, separable morphology and<br/>separable Gaussian are all ordinary render passes into small textures, so none of it needed a compute shader"]

  subgraph DIV["THE THREE GENUINE DIVERGENCES — and they are the whole list"]
    D1["1 · PER-OBJECT RECORDS<br/>WebGPU: a read-only storage buffer · WebGL2: an RGBA32F texture read with texelFetch<br/>GLES 3.0 has no storage buffers, and a 16 KB UBO would hold about fifty of a 304-byte mesh record<br/>every stride is a multiple of 16 bytes, so a record is a whole number of texels — 19 of them for mesh<br/>u32 fields are written as plain floats, since 2u read back through a float texture is a denormal some GPUs flush to zero"]
    D2["2 · WHERE THE MULTISAMPLING COMES FROM<br/>WebGPU: a multisampled texture that resolves into the swapchain when the pass ends<br/>WebGL2: the browser's own multisampled drawing buffer — one blit and one colour buffer fewer per frame<br/>antialias true is a hint, so Gl2Context.sampleCount reports what was granted, not what was asked for"]
    D3["3 · RENDER-TO-TEXTURE ORIENTATION<br/>WebGPU puts NDC y = +1 in a texture's FIRST texel row, GL in its LAST<br/>corrected in exactly two places, and pinned by webgl/webgl.test.ts<br/>because getting one without the other gives upside-down shadows"]
  end

  SCALE["WHAT ACTUALLY DIFFERS FOR A USER IS SCALE<br/>hundreds of thousands of objects on the primary path, tens of thousands on the fallback<br/>backend webgl2 forces it, because a fallback nobody can reach on purpose is a fallback nobody tests"]

